---
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";
---

<Layout title="Careers" description="Join the Junior Hub team. Current openings and how to apply.">
    <section id="banner">
      <h2>
        <b><span style="color: white; font-size: 125">Careers</span></b>
      </h2>
    </section>

    <!-- Main -->
    <section id="main" class="container">
      <section class="box special">
        <span class="image featured"
          ><img src="/images/pic01.jpeg" alt=""
        /></span>
        <p>
          Junior Hub Child Care and Learning Centre is located in the
          neighborhood of Hwy 7, 407 and Yonge Street, providing full-time
          care for children from 18mons to 6 years of age. We offer rewarding
          careers for dynamic professionals who are committed to life-long
          learning. We are currently recruiting highly motivated and
          responsible individuals to join our team.
        </p>
        <h3 style="font-weight: bold; text-align: center">
          Registered Early Childhood Educator (RECE)
        </h3>
        <p>
          Reporting to: Supervisor
          <br />
          <br />
          Successful candidates will have:
        </p>
        <ul style="text-align: left">
          <li>
            Registration in good standing with the College of Early Childhood
            Educators
          </li>
          <li>
            Working knowledge of Child Care and Early Years Act, ELECT, and
            HDLH
          </li>
          <li>
            Strong ability to plan, implement and document developmentally
            appropriate and bias-free activities with understanding of ELECT
            and How Does Learning Happen?; to engage with children to support
            their development in all areas; to organize an inspirational
            learning environment.
          </li>
          <li>
            Proven ability to communicate in a professional manner with
            children, parents/guardians, and staff
          </li>
          <li>
            Excellent work ethics (be punctual, flexible, reliable) and
            commitment to quality care
          </li>
          <li>
            Current standard First Aid and CPR, clear Police Records Check
            with Vulnerable Sector Check dated within 6 months of hire date,
            Up-to-date health assessment including TB test.
          </li>
        </ul>

        <h3 style="font-weight: bold; text-align: center">
          Early Childhood Assistants (ECA)
        </h3>
        <p>Successful candidates will have:</p>
        <ul style="text-align: left">
          <li>
            Minimum of six months’ experience working with children in a day
            care or before and after school program
          </li>
          <li>An ECA Diploma as an asset</li>
          <li>
            Ability to engage with children to support their development in
            all areas; to maintain and clean an inspirational learning
            environment
          </li>

          <li>
            Proven ability to communicate in a professional manner with
            children, parents/guardians, and staff
          </li>
          <li>
            Excellent work ethics (be punctual, flexible, reliable) and
            commitment to quality care
          </li>
          <li>
            Current standard First Aid and CPR, clear Police Records Check
            with Vulnerable Sector Check dated within 6 months of hire date,
            Up-to-date health assessment including TB test.
          </li>
        </ul>

        <h3 style="font-weight: bold; text-align: center">
          Montessori Teacher
        </h3>
        <p>
          Reporting to: Supervisor
          <br />
          <br />
          Successful candidates will have:
        </p>
        <ul style="text-align: left">
          <li>
            Diploma in Montessori Training from an accredited Montessori
            Training Institute
          </li>
          <li>
            At least one year of on-job experience working in a Montessori
            environment
          </li>
          <li>
            Experience to observe, guide and assess children while they learn
            in the classroom environment; to plan and implement Montessori
            learning activities to children; to engage with children to
            support their development in all areas
          </li>

          <li>
            Proven ability to communicate in a professional manner with
            children, parents/guardians, and staff
          </li>
          <li>
            Excellent work ethics (be punctual, flexible, reliable) and
            commitment to quality care
          </li>
          <li>
            Current standard First Aid and CPR, clear Police Records Check
            with Vulnerable Sector Check dated within 6 months of hire date,
            Up-to-date health assessment including TB test.
          </li>
        </ul>

        <p>
          Please email your résumé to
          <a href="mailto:info@juniorhub.ca">info@juniorhub.ca</a> with the
          email header of the role and your name. Thank you for your interest.
          Only applicants selected for an interview will be contacted.
        </p>
      </section>
    </section>
</Layout>
